<title>PHILIPPINES: Wing Tiek completes Manila steel firm sale.</title>
<headline>Wing Tiek completes Manila steel firm sale.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hottic Investments Ltd, a Hong Kong-based firm, had formally acquired 82.5 percent of the Philippines' National Steel Corp (NSC) with the payment of $800 million to Wing Tiek Holdings Bhd, NSC said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>The payment completed all obligations of former majority owner Wing Tiek due to the Philippine government. It also fulfilled the balance of equity holdings due to NSC, the statement said.</p>
<p>The formerly state-owned NSC was acquired by Wing Tiek last year but later decided to sell it.</p>
</text>
